.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH acc-pr 1  "pr 0.5.4" 
.SH NAME
acc\-pr \- Collect and evaluate one pull request
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBacc pr\fR [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-policy\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-agent\-account\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-agent\-trailer\fR] [\fB\-\-ignore\-trailers\fR] [\fB\-\-agent\-trace\fR] [\fB\-\-attestations\fR] [\fB\-\-verified\-by\fR] [\fB\-\-verification\fR] [\fB\-\-agent\-vendor\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-pages\fR] [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fINUMBER\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Collect and evaluate one pull request
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress status lines on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<OWNER/REPO>\fR
Repository as OWNER/REPO; defaults to GITHUB_REPOSITORY, else the github.com origin remote of the working directory
.TP
\fB\-\-policy\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Policy file (defaults to .agent\-change\-control/policy.yml when present)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print extra diagnostics on stderr (resolved policy, format, destination, counts). Never changes stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-agent\-account\fR \fI<LOGIN=AGENT>\fR
Treat LOGIN as the verified account of AGENT (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Never color diagnostics. acc\*(Aqs own output is never colored; this and a non\-empty NO_COLOR environment variable switch off color in help and usage errors too
.TP
\fB\-\-agent\-trailer\fR \fI<EMAIL=AGENT>\fR
Treat commits whose Co\-Authored\-By trailer carries EMAIL as written by AGENT (repeatable; extends the built\-in vendor registry)
.TP
\fB\-\-ignore\-trailers\fR
Do not read Co\-Authored\-By trailers; only declarations and account mappings establish agent authorship
.TP
\fB\-\-agent\-trace\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Agent Trace record files or directories, bound to commits by vcs.revision (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-attestations\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Attestation files or directories (in\-toto Statements, DSSE envelopes or Sigstore bundles, .json or .jsonl), bound to changes by their head commit (repeatable). acc does not verify signatures; see \-\-verified\-by
.TP
\fB\-\-verified\-by\fR \fI<TEXT>\fR
Who verified the attestations\*(Aq signatures before this run, recorded verbatim (for example "gh attestation verify, run 123"). Without it attestation claims count as declared, not signed
.TP
\fB\-\-verification\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
A verifier\*(Aqs JSON output (`gh attestation verify \-\-format json`): its bundles are loaded as signed attestations with the certificate identity the verifier established (repeatable; requires \-\-verified\-by)
.TP
\fB\-\-agent\-vendor\fR \fI<AGENT=VENDOR>\fR
Treat AGENT as built and operated by VENDOR (repeatable; extends the built\-in registry)
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-pages\fR \fI<N>\fR [default: 100]
Maximum pages per list endpoint (100 items each)
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR
Output format; inferred from the \-\-output extension when omitted
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
yaml
.IP \(bu 2
table: A plain\-text table for people; `text` is an alias
.IP \(bu 2
sarif
.IP \(bu 2
in\-toto: An unsigned in\-toto Statement v1 whose predicate is the manifest
.IP \(bu 2
in\-toto\-jsonl: JSON Lines of unsigned in\-toto Statements, one per change
.RE
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Write to FILE instead of stdout
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fINUMBER\fR>
Pull request number
.SH VERSION
v0.5.4
